# POSTGRESQL DATA RULES
- Use PostgreSQL with UTF-8 encoding. Migration names: `create_{table}_table`, `add_{col}_to_{table}_table`.
- Money = `decimal(15,2)`; percentages = `unsignedTinyInteger` / smallint (0-100); booleans = `boolean`; long text = `text`.
- Column lengths follow SRS 7.1 (e.g. last_name 80, first_name 40, company 255, opportunity name 120).
- Foreign keys with explicit `onDelete` (restrict by default; cascade only where the SRS says child records cascade).
- Index every FK, every owner_id, status/stage, due_date, close_date, and searchable columns (name, email, company, case_number).
- Polymorphic Task/Event relations: `related_to_type` + `related_to_id` via `morphs()`; register a `Relation::morphMap`
  (lead, account, contact, opportunity, case) so raw class names are never stored.
- Account self-reference `parent_account_id`; Contact self-reference `reports_to_id`.
- Lead keeps converted_account_id / converted_contact_id / converted_opportunity_id.
- Case number: auto-generated, unique. Opportunity `is_closed`, `is_won`, `expected_revenue` derive from stage/amount x probability.
- Archive (soft delete) Opportunities as required; use SoftDeletes wherever the SRS says "archive".
- Seeders: roles/permissions, picklists (lead status/source, industries, stages + probabilities), demo data (NFR-USE-005).
- Test with a PostgreSQL test database (not SQLite, not MySQL) so behaviour matches production.
- Never introduce MySQL-specific SQL, engines (InnoDB), or drivers; use portable Eloquent/Query Builder or PostgreSQL-compatible SQL only.
